   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain contracts\nof the New York city school construction authority; and to amend chapter 738\nof the laws of 1988 amending the administrative code of the city of New York\nand other laws relating to establishing the New York city school construction\nauthority, in relation to extending certain provisions of such chapter\nrelating to certain contracts of the New York city school construction\nauthority",
    "basePrintNo": "S9347",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9347-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1735, Pub Auth L; amd §19, Chap 738 of 1988",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9347\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain\ncontracts of the New York city school construction authority; and to\namend chapter 738 of the laws of 1988 amending the administrative code\nof the city of New York and other laws relating to establishing the New\nYork city school construction authority, in relation to extending\ncertain provisions of such chapter relating to certain contracts of the\nNew York city school construction authority\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill extends until 2019 the exemption of New York City school\nconstruction authority from Section 101 of the General Municipal Law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROMIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 1735 of the public authorities law to extend\nthe exemption of the school construction authority (SCA) from Section\n101 of the General Municipal Law to June 30, 2028.  The SCA has been\nexempt from Section 101 of the General Municipal Law since 1988. The\nexemption is necessary for ongoing construction projects that the city's\nschool construction authority is undertaking to address overcrowding in\npublic schools. If the exemption lapses, the school\n\nSection 2 amends Section 19 of Chapter 738 of the Laws of 1988 also to\nextend the exemption until 2028.\n\nSection 3 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nconstruction authority will have to suspend its operations and project\nlabor agreements with the construction unions. This disruption will\ndelay the creation of new public school seats and leave New York City\nschool children In overcrowded public schools.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nJuly 1, 2024\n",
